Package: WeGrowHealthR
Type: Package
Title: Child Growth Data Analysis, Modelling and Reproducible Workflows
Version: 1.0.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Nhan Thi", "Ho", email = "nhanhocumc@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c("MD, PhD", ORCID = "0000-0002-7898-0956")))
Description: Tools and one-call workflows for longitudinal child growth data,
    written to accompany the books 'Child Growth Data Analysis and Modeling
    with R' and its advanced companion. The package covers data cleaning,
    World Health Organization and US Centers for Disease Control and
    Prevention z-scores, percentiles and nutritional status, prevalence
    and trend analysis, mixed-model trajectories, SuperImposition by
    Translation And Rotation (SITAR) growth curves and the pubertal spurt
    (Cole, Donaldson and Ben-Shlomo (2010) <doi:10.1093/ije/dyq115>),
    quantile regression and linear quantile mixed models for growth
    distributions (Geraci (2014) <doi:10.18637/jss.v057.i13>), conditional
    growth references, functional growth phenotypes, canalization and
    multistate models, prediction model benchmarks with SHapley Additive
    exPlanations (SHAP), and a simulation engine that produces teaching
    cohorts with known truth. Established engines such as 'sitar',
    'quantreg', 'lqmm', 'msm', 'fdapace' and 'mclust' do the fitting, and
    the package adds growth-specific data handling, cluster bootstraps,
    safeguards, reproducible parallel computing and publication output.
    One-call workflows reproduce the analyses of a research program on the
    growth of urban schoolchildren.
